    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d661">

                <pb facs="1136" n="1036" sameAs="frus:frus1880/pg1036"/>

                <head>No. 661.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Baker to Mr. Evarts.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Caracas</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1880-04-19"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 19, 1880</date>.
                        (Received May 6.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 219.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I think it proper to communicate to you, as
                    matter of information, that Mr. C. J. Bandman (of New York, I think) has
                    contracted with this government for the construction and operation of two
                    prospective railways: one from La Guayra to Caracas, and the other from Puerto
                    Cabello to Valencia.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * *</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JEHU BAKER.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
